<?php init_head(); ?><div id="wrapper"><div class="content"><div class="panel_s"><div class="panel-body"><?php $this->load->view("_navigation"); ?>
<div class="sdp-guide-intro"><h3><i class="fa fa-book"></i> Smart Daily Productivity — Employee Guide</h3><p>A practical guide to recording your daily work, reviewing your hours, and understanding productivity reports.</p></div>
<div class="sdp-guide-grid">
<section class="sdp-guide-card"><span class="sdp-guide-number">01</span><h4>Submit your daily work</h4><p>Open <strong>My Day Report</strong>, choose the work date, and create a separate entry for each activity. Include the activity title, category, minutes, and a clear description.</p><div class="sdp-example"><strong>Example</strong><p><b>Activity:</b> Prepare customer estimate<br><b>Time:</b> 90 minutes<br><b>Notes:</b> Reviewed drawings, calculated materials, and sent the estimate for approval.</p></div></section>
<section class="sdp-guide-card"><span class="sdp-guide-number">02</span><h4>Write useful progress notes</h4><p>Explain what was completed, what is still pending, and whether someone else must take action. Specific notes help managers understand your work.</p><div class="sdp-example"><strong>Example</strong><p><b>Completed:</b> Called three suppliers.<br><b>Pending:</b> Waiting for two written quotes.<br><b>Next step:</b> Follow up tomorrow morning.</p></div></section>
<section class="sdp-guide-card"><span class="sdp-guide-number">03</span><h4>Review your entries and hours</h4><p>Use the date filter in <strong>My Day Report</strong> to find entries. Select <strong>View</strong> for the full details. If your role allows editing, correct manual entries as needed.</p><div class="sdp-example"><strong>Example</strong><p>Two entries of 60 and 45 minutes equal 105 minutes, or 1.75 hours of recorded work.</p></div></section>
<section class="sdp-guide-card"><span class="sdp-guide-number">04</span><h4>Understand dashboard numbers</h4><p><b>Entries</b> counts logged activities; <b>Total Hours</b> sums recorded minutes; <b>Tasks</b> and <b>Tickets</b> reflect captured CRM activity; <b>Manual</b> counts employee-submitted entries.</p><div class="sdp-example"><strong>Example</strong><p>Four manual entries and two automatic task events can produce six recorded entries, depending on the date filter.</p></div></section>
<section class="sdp-guide-card"><span class="sdp-guide-number">05</span><h4>Manager reports and comparisons</h4><p>Authorized managers can open <strong>Reports</strong>, choose dates, and select two or more employees. Use the horizontal progress bars and doughnut chart to compare scores. Click an employee's name to inspect their daily work.</p><div class="sdp-example"><strong>Example</strong><p>Select Camila and Jannatul for the same week, then review their recorded activities and time spent. Scores are not a substitute for reviewing work quality.</p></div></section>
<section class="sdp-guide-card"><span class="sdp-guide-number">06</span><h4>Permissions and missing activities</h4><p>Employees can view their own work when authorized. Other employees' reports require the <strong>Reports</strong> permission. If an activity is missing, first check the date and then add a manual entry if allowed.</p><div class="sdp-example"><strong>Example</strong><p>If a customer call does not appear automatically, record the call with its duration and outcome. A missing entry does not prove no work occurred.</p></div></section>
</div><div class="panel_s"><div class="panel-body"><h3><i class="fa fa-bell"></i> Daily Reminders and Audio Alarms</h3><p>Open <strong>Smart Daily Productivity → Daily Reminders</strong> or click the orange <strong>Daily Reminder</strong> button on the dashboard. Enter the title, instructions, reminder date and time, and select an alarm. Save to add it to your personal reminder list.</p><p>Upload your MP3 audio files to <code>media/Alarms/</code> inside the CRM installation directory. Name them exactly <code>alarm 1.mp3</code> (food break) and <code>alarm 2.mp3</code> (other reminders). Names are case-sensitive on Linux hosting.</p><p>Keep the Daily Reminders page open to receive popup and audio alerts. Browsers may block automatic audio until you interact with the page. This release does not send alarms when the browser is closed. Click <strong>Mark Complete</strong> after responding to a reminder.</p></div></div>
<div class="panel_s"><div class="panel-body"><h3><i class="fa fa-check-square-o"></i> Daily Task Checklist</h3><p>Open <strong>Smart Daily Productivity → Daily Task Checklist</strong>, or click <strong>Daily Task Checklist</strong> on the dashboard. Use <strong>Add or Edit Daily Task</strong> to create recurring responsibilities such as checking email, reviewing estimates, or submitting reports.</p><p>Use <strong>Add Sample Daily Tasks</strong> on the checklist to import eight editable examples without duplicates. This is optional and does not replace any existing list. Employees check the square beside each completed task. Checkmarks are saved separately for each date, so tomorrow starts with a fresh checklist while previous days remain available through the date picker. Click <strong>Edit</strong> to change the task title or instructions. Use the Daily Reminders tab for scheduled audio alerts; checklist items and timed reminders are separate features.</p><p>Audio files belong in <code>media/Alarms/</code>: <code>alarm 1.mp3</code> for food breaks and <code>alarm 2.mp3</code> for other reminders. The reminders page must remain open for browser audio alerts.</p></div></div><div class="alert alert-info"><i class="fa fa-info-circle"></i> For help with corrections or permissions, contact your manager. Always back up the CRM database and module files before an upgrade.</div>
</div></div></div></div><div class="panel_s"><div class="panel-body"><h3>Daily Reminders — Employee Checklist</h3><p>Open <strong>Smart Daily Productivity → Daily Reminders</strong> to view recurring responsibilities. Check a task when finished. The progress bar updates for the selected day; the next day starts unchecked.</p><h4>Manage Daily Tasks</h4><p>Open <strong>Manage Daily Tasks</strong> to create, edit or pause recurring tasks. This is separate from the employee checklist.</p><h4>Audio Alarms</h4><p>Open <strong>Audio Alarms</strong> for timed notifications. Upload <code>alarm 1.mp3</code> (food break) and <code>alarm 2.mp3</code> (other alarms) to <code>media/Alarms/</code>. Audio plays only while the relevant page is open and browser playback is permitted.</p><h4>Daily Work Report</h4><p>After checking tasks, open <strong>My Day Report</strong> to submit the work completed, blockers and notes. A checked task does not automatically submit a daily report.</p></div></div>
